Rust crates built into the HyperFlux Next programs

The HyperFlux Next programs in this package include code from the Rust
crates below, downloaded from crates.io. Every one of them may be used
under the MIT license; most also offer Apache-2.0 and memchr also offers
the Unlicense. HyperFlux Next uses each of them under the MIT license.
Each crate's own MIT license, with its copyright notice, follows.

Crates in the build that are not part of the programs:
- proc-macro2 1.0.107: used only while compiling
- quote 1.0.47: used only while compiling
- serde_derive 1.0.229: used only while compiling
- syn 3.0.2: used only while compiling
- unicode-ident 1.0.24: used only while compiling
- windows-link 0.2.1: built only for Windows
- windows-sys 0.61.2: built only for Windows

